            <div xml:id="d515">

                <pb facs="0564" n="466" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg466"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003/411: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-09-10T11:00:00+08:00">September 10, 1930—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 10—3 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>796. Your 312, September 8, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="64" xml:id="d515-f1"/> paragraph 3.
                    Lampson showed me text of formula for Hankow, Tientsin and Canton. I did not
                    take a copy. My recollection is that formula for Hankow and Canton was similar
                    to that for Shanghai, while Tientsin formula was altered to cover activity at
                    Tangku.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
